{
  "message": "I’m here to help. To fix a “No Service” issue, I’ll first verify your account and line status to rule out things like a suspension or SIM provisioning issue, then guide you through quick device checks (airplane mode, SIM status, network mode, APN) with reasons for each step. Please provide one of the following so I can locate your account and the affected line.",
  "requested_verification": {
    "provide_one_of": [
      "Phone number for the affected line",
      "Customer ID",
      "Full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD)"
    ]
  },
  "additional_questions": [
    "Is the issue happening everywhere you go, or only in a specific location?",
    "Did anything change recently (new phone/SIM/eSIM transfer, plan change, software update)?",
    "Do you see an Airplane Mode icon on the status bar, or was Airplane Mode turned on recently?",
    "Do others around you on the same carrier have service?",
    "What phone model are you using?"
  ],
  "next_steps_explained": "After I identify your account, I will check your line status for any suspensions or provisioning issues. If the line is okay, I’ll guide you to confirm Airplane Mode is off, check SIM status, ensure the phone’s network mode isn’t limited to 2G/3G, verify APN if needed, and try a reboot. Each step helps isolate whether it’s account, network, or device configuration related."
}

