messages.content:
{
  "message": "I can help. Since you’re abroad, we’ll do two things in parallel: (1) check your account/line to ensure international data roaming is enabled and you’re not out of data, and (2) run quick on‑device checks to restore the fastest possible speed. I can’t change settings on your phone remotely, so I’ll guide you step by step. First, please identify your account so I can look up your line: • What is the mobile phone number on the SIM you’re using right now (include country code, e.g., +33 or +1)? While you share that, please run these quick checks on your phone and paste the exact results back here: 1) check_network_status — I need: Airplane mode (On/Off), Signal strength (none/poor/fair/good/excellent), Network type (e.g., 5G/4G/3G/2G), Mobile data (On/Off), Data roaming (On/Off). 2) check_status_bar — Note any icons such as ✈️, network type (5G/4G), bars, or an R/roaming indicator. 3) run_speed_test — Share the result (no connection/very poor/poor/fair/good/excellent). If it’s quicker for you, you can also manually verify these settings now: • Airplane Mode: OFF • Mobile Data: ON • Data Roaming: ON (required abroad) • Network Mode: 4G/5G preferred • Data Saver: OFF • VPN: OFF After that, if possible, reboot the phone and try again. Once you provide your number, I’ll verify your line’s roaming setting and data balance. If roaming isn’t enabled on the line, I can enable it at no cost (with your consent). If you’re out of plan data, we can add up to 2 GB of refuel data immediately or discuss plan options. Note: We’ll aim for the best available speed in your area, but final speed depends on local networks. Please share your phone number and the diagnostic results, and we’ll proceed."
}

