messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for confirming the network mode. Since data is refueled and Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF, the next most common blockers are Data Saver/background restrictions, an active VPN, app permissions, or a corrupted APN profile. Please keep Wi‑Fi OFF during these tests so MMS uses cellular data. After each step, try sending an MMS and stop if it works.",
  "steps": [
    "Check Data Saver/background restrictions: run check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON or global background data is restricted, turn it OFF using toggle_data_saver_mode, then try sending an MMS.",
    "Check VPN: run check_vpn_status. If a VPN is active/connected, use disconnect_vpn, then try sending an MMS.",
    "Confirm messaging app permissions: run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\"). If “storage” or “sms” aren’t granted, grant them with grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\") and grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\"), then try sending an MMS.",
    "Refresh APN profile: even though MMSC is present, reset the APN to clear any corruption. Run reset_apn_settings, then reboot_device. After the phone restarts, ensure Mobile Data is ON (and Wi‑Fi OFF), then try sending an MMS.",
    "Optional diagnostic: run can_send_mms and share the result if the send still fails."
  ],
  "request": {
    "confirm_results": [
      "Data Saver status before/after and MMS send result",
      "VPN status and whether you disconnected it; MMS result",
      "Messaging app permissions (whether storage and sms were granted) and MMS result",
      "Whether you reset APN + rebooted; MMS result afterward",
      "If still failing: the result of can_send_mms"
    ]
  }
}

