messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for checking. Seeing “No Signal” with “Data Disabled” means your phone currently isn’t connected to the cellular network, so MMS cannot work yet. We’ll first restore basic service and data, then re-test MMS.",
  "why": "MMS requires both cellular service and mobile data. No signal prevents any MMS, and data must be ON once service returns.",
  "requested_account_verification": "Before we go too far, please share ONE of the following so I can also check your line status (e.g., suspension or roaming): 1) The phone number for the affected line, OR 2) Your customer ID, OR 3) Your full name and date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Check/Toggle Airplane Mode",
      "instructions": "If you see an airplane icon, turn Airplane Mode OFF. If you don’t see it, toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then OFF to refresh all radios."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reseat the SIM",
      "instructions": "Power the phone off. Remove the SIM tray, ensure the SIM is clean and properly aligned, then reinsert it firmly. Power the phone back on."
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn Mobile Data ON",
      "instructions": "After the phone restarts, turn Mobile Data ON. Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for this test so we can confirm cellular data is working."
    },
    {
      "title": "Set Network Mode to modern networks",
      "instructions": "Ensure your preferred network mode is set to include 4G/5G (e.g., “4G/5G preferred”). Avoid 2G/3G-only modes."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reboot once more",
      "instructions": "Restart the phone to apply any network/SIM changes cleanly."
    },
    {
      "title": "Re-check the status bar and test MMS",
      "instructions": "Confirm you now see signal bars and a 4G/LTE/5G indicator, and that Mobile Data shows as enabled. Then try sending an MMS (a small photo) to yourself."
    }
  ],
  "ask_to_report_back": "Please tell me: 1) Do you now see signal bars and a network type (4G/LTE/5G)? 2) Is Mobile Data ON? 3) Did the MMS send successfully, or what error do you see?",
  "questions": [
    "What’s the phone model (Android or iPhone)?",
    "Are you currently traveling outside your usual coverage area or internationally?",
    "Did MMS work on this device before today, and did anything change recently (new SIM/phone, settings, VPN)?"
  ],
  "next_actions_after_you_reply": "With your phone number or account details, I will check your line for any suspension or roaming settings that could block service, and we’ll proceed to APN/MMSC checks if needed."
}

