messages.content:
{
  "message": "Great—service and mobile data are back. Since MMS still won’t send, the next most common causes are APN/MMSC settings, Wi‑Fi Calling conflicts, missing app permissions, VPN interference, or Data Saver. We’ll check each quickly and retest.",
  "requested_account_verification": "Please also share ONE of the following so I can check your line on our side while you try the steps: 1) The phone number for the affected line, OR 2) Your customer ID, OR 3) Your full name and date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Verify APN has an MMSC URL (required for MMS)",
      "why": "If the MMSC is missing/incorrect, MMS will fail even with good data.",
      "instructions": "On the phone, run check_apn_settings and tell me: • Current APN name • MMSC URL. If MMSC is missing or looks wrong, run reset_apn_settings, then run reboot_device. After the reboot, try sending a small photo MMS to yourself with Wi‑Fi OFF."
    },
    {
      "title": "Disable Wi‑Fi Calling (temporarily)",
      "why": "Some setups block MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling.",
      "instructions": "Run check_wifi_calling_status. If it shows ON, run toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF. Keep Wi‑Fi OFF and test MMS again."
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm messaging app permissions",
      "why": "MMS needs storage (to attach media) and SMS permissions.",
      "instructions": "Run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\"). If storage or sms are NOT granted, run grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\") and grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\"). Test MMS again."
    },
    {
      "title": "Ensure no VPN is active",
      "why": "VPNs can interfere with MMS routing.",
      "instructions": "Run check_vpn_status. If connected, run disconnect_vpn. Test MMS again."
    },
    {
      "title": "Make sure Data Saver is OFF",
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict background data and break MMS in some apps.",
      "instructions": "Run check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF. Test MMS again."
    },
    {
      "title": "Quick capability check",
      "why": "Confirms the device believes it can send MMS after changes.",
      "instructions": "Run can_send_mms. Share the result, then try sending one more test MMS to yourself with Wi‑Fi OFF."
    }
  ],
  "ask_to_report_back": "Please tell me: 1) What did check_apn_settings show for MMSC? 2) Was Wi‑Fi Calling ON, and did turning it OFF help? 3) Were storage/sms permissions missing, and did you grant them? 4) Was a VPN connected? 5) Is Data Saver ON or OFF? 6) What did can_send_mms report? 7) When you try to send, do you see an error message or does it just spin/time out?",
  "questions": [
    "What phone model and OS (Android or iPhone)?",
    "Which messaging app are you using (default Messages, Google Messages, etc.)?"
  ],
  "next_actions_after_you_reply": "If MMSC was missing or we changed settings, we’ll re-verify after reboot. With your phone number or customer ID, I’ll also check your line on our side (roaming setting, any blocks) to rule out account-level causes."
}

