messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for checking—an empty MMSC confirms why MMS is failing. MMS requires a valid MMSC URL in the APN. The fastest, safe fix is to reset the APN to carrier defaults and then reboot so the correct MMSC is applied.",
  "thought_process": "Because your signal and mobile data are excellent, the radio/network are fine. The missing MMSC is a configuration issue. Resetting APN + reboot forces the phone to reload the carrier profile. After that, we verify the MMSC is populated and re-test MMS. If it still fails, we’ll rule out Wi‑Fi Calling conflicts, app permissions, VPN/Data Saver, and finally escalate if the MMSC won’t populate.",
  "requested_account_verification": "Please also provide ONE of the following so I can check your line on our side while you try the steps: 1) The phone number for the affected line, OR 2) Your customer ID, OR 3) Your full name and date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Reset APN to defaults",
      "why": "Populates the correct MMSC from your carrier profile.",
      "instructions": "On the phone, run reset_apn_settings. This reverts APN/MMSC to defaults."
    },
    {
      "title": "Reboot to apply",
      "why": "Changes don’t fully apply until after a restart.",
      "instructions": "Run reboot_device. Wait for the phone to fully power back on."
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify MMSC and test MMS",
      "why": "Confirms the fix took effect.",
      "instructions": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF. Run check_apn_settings and confirm the MMSC URL is now present (non-empty, starts with http/https). Then, try sending a small photo MMS to yourself."
    },
    {
      "title": "If MMSC is still blank, rule out other blockers",
      "why": "Occasionally other settings interfere.",
      "instructions": "• Run check_wifi_calling_status; if ON, run toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF and retest MMS. • Run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\"); if storage or sms aren’t granted, run grant_app_permission for each, then retest. • Run check_vpn_status; if connected, run disconnect_vpn, then retest. • Run check_data_restriction_status; if Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF, then retest."
    },
    {
      "title": "Capability check",
      "why": "See if the device believes MMS can work after changes.",
      "instructions": "Run can_send_mms and share the result with me."
    }
  ],
  "ask_to_report_back": "Please tell me: 1) After the reset + reboot, is the MMSC now populated? 2) Did the MMS send successfully with Wi‑Fi OFF? 3) If not, what were the results of the Wi‑Fi Calling, permissions, VPN, and Data Saver checks? 4) What did can_send_mms report?",
  "next_actions_after_you_reply": "If the MMSC populates and MMS still fails, we’ll continue with targeted checks. If the MMSC remains blank after reset+reboot, I’ll arrange further assistance to push the correct carrier profile. I’ll also review your line on our side once you share your phone number or customer ID."
}

