  "summary": "You have good 4G signal and mobile data enabled, but no data or MMS. Roaming is enabled and APN was reset, so this is likely a network selection/roaming partner issue on the device side. We’ll switch networks and re-register. If that doesn’t work, we’ll reseat the SIM.",
  "next_steps_on_android_in_order": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Set Network Selection to Automatic",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Network operators > Select automatically.",
      "why": "Ensures the phone picks a compatible roaming partner."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "If still no data, try Manual Network Selection",
      "how": "In the same Network operators screen, turn OFF automatic and wait for the list of networks to load. Try one at a time: Orange F, SFR, Bouygues Telecom, Free Mobile (names may vary slightly). After selecting each network:",
      "after_select": [
        "Wait 20–30 seconds for registration.",
        "Briefly toggle Airplane Mode ON for 5 seconds, then OFF.",
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF, Mobile Data ON, Data Roaming ON.",
        "Try loading a webpage and then sending a small MMS."
      ],
      "tip": "If one network allows calls/SMS but still no data, try the next network."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "Allow fallback beyond LTE-only",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Preferred network type > choose 5G/4G/3G/2G (Auto) or 4G/3G/2G (Auto) instead of LTE-only.",
      "why": "Some roaming partners may pass data on 3G/4G but fail on LTE-only. Auto lets the phone pick what works."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Quick data refresh toggles",
      "how": [
        "Toggle Mobile Data OFF, wait 5 seconds, then ON.",
        "Toggle Airplane Mode ON for 5 seconds, then OFF."
      ],
      "why": "Forces re-registration after mode/operator changes."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Reseat the SIM (if still no data)",
      "how": "Power OFF the phone. Remove the SIM tray and SIM, wait 10–20 seconds, reinsert firmly, then power ON.",
      "after": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF, Mobile Data ON, Data Roaming ON. Wait 30–60 seconds, then try a webpage and an MMS again.",
      "why": "Fixes registration issues caused by a marginal SIM contact."
    }
  ],
  "please_report_back": [
    "Which operator is currently selected (Automatic, Orange, SFR, Bouygues, or Free)?",
    "What does the top bar show now (e.g., 4G/5G and an ‘R’)?",
    "After trying each operator and the auto mode, did any webpage load?",
    "Did any MMS send?",
    "If something failed, which step and exactly what you saw (any error messages or icons)?"
  ],
  "thought_process": "Roaming is enabled on your line and you have 2 GB of added data. APN is reset and Data Saver/VPN are off, so the remaining common blocker is the specific roaming partner/network your phone latched onto. Manually switching operators and allowing multiple network technologies typically resolves this. If these steps fail, we’ll consider further actions like SIM reseat (included above) and, if still no data, escalate to a human agent to check roaming provisioning with partners."
}

