messages.content:
{
  "reply": "Thanks for the thorough checks—your connection, network mode, APN/MMSC, Wi‑Fi Calling, and VPN all look good. The next most common causes are a device-side restriction or the messaging app lacking a needed permission. I’ll guide you step by step. It’s safe to try these; I’ll explain why each helps.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "MMS relies on mobile data and the messaging app’s ability to access storage/SMS. Even with great data, Data Saver or missing app permissions can silently block MMS.",
    "A quick data toggle and a reboot refresh cellular services and the MMS stack.",
    "APN reset (with reboot) can fix hidden APN fields even when the visible MMSC looks correct."
  ],
  "steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Confirm mobile data is being used",
      "do_this": [
        "Ensure Wi‑Fi is still OFF.",
        "Make sure the airplane icon is gone."
      ],
      "reason": "We want MMS to use mobile data."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check Data Saver / background restrictions",
      "run": "check_data_restriction_status",
      "if_result": {
        "data_saver_on": {
          "action": "toggle_data_saver_mode (turn OFF)",
          "then": "Retry sending an MMS to your own number."
        }
      },
      "reason": "Data Saver can block background transfers that MMS needs."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check messaging app permissions",
      "run": "check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\")",
      "look_for": [
        "storage (or photos/media/files)",
        "sms"
      ],
      "if_missing": [
        "grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\")",
        "grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\")"
      ],
      "then": "Retry sending an MMS.",
      "reason": "Without storage/SMS permissions, the app can fail to attach/send pictures."
    },
    {
      "step": "Quick network refresh",
      "do_this": [
        "toggle_data (turn OFF), wait 10 seconds, then toggle_data (turn ON)."
      ],
      "then": "Retry sending an MMS.",
      "reason": "Refreshes the data session the MMS service uses."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reboot the device",
      "run": "reboot_device",
      "then": "After the phone restarts, keep Wi‑Fi OFF and try sending an MMS again.",
      "reason": "Clears any temporary MMS or radio stack glitches."
    },
    {
      "step": "APN reset (only if still failing after the above)",
      "run": [
        "reset_apn_settings",
        "reboot_device (required after APN reset)"
      ],
      "then": "With Wi‑Fi OFF, try sending an MMS again.",
      "reason": "Resets hidden APN fields related to MMS that may not show visibly."
    },
    {
      "step": "Optional hardware refresh if still failing",
      "run": "reseat_sim_card",
      "then": "Wait for service to return, verify 4G/5G shows, and try MMS again.",
      "reason": "Reinitializes SIM/network provisioning on the device."
    }
  ],
  "please_share_back": [
    "Results of check_data_restriction_status (was Data Saver ON or OFF?).",
    "Results of check_app_permissions for your messaging app (were storage/SMS missing, and did granting help?).",
    "After the data toggle and reboot, did an MMS to your own number send?",
    "If you performed the APN reset + reboot, did that resolve it?"
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Which phone and messaging app are you using (e.g., Android with Google Messages/Samsung Messages, or iPhone Messages)?",
    "After turning off Wi‑Fi and confirming Airplane Mode is off, do you see 4G/LTE/5G with signal bars now?"
  ],
  "next_step_note": "If MMS still fails after all the above, I’ll escalate with all findings so a specialist can investigate deeper app/device-specific behavior. Let me know each result so I can decide the exact next action."
}

