  "thought_process": "Right now your phone shows no signal and mobile data OFF, so MMS cannot work. Since you’re abroad and your account has roaming enabled, the most likely causes are: the phone hasn’t attached to a roaming network yet, mobile data/roaming is OFF on the phone, or the network mode is set too low (e.g., 2G). We’ll force a fresh network attach, enable data and roaming on the phone, and ensure the preferred network mode supports 4G/5G.",
  "step_by_step_actions": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "action": "toggle_airplane_mode",
      "how": "Turn Airplane Mode ON for ~15 seconds, then turn it OFF.",
      "why": "This forces the phone to re-register with available roaming networks.",
      "what_to_check_after": "Look at the status bar again. Do you now see any signal bars and a network type (3G/4G/LTE/5G) or an 'R' for roaming?"
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "action": "toggle_data",
      "how": "Turn Mobile Data ON in your phone settings.",
